statement:
For a convex hexagon $ABCDEF$ in which each pair of opposite sides is unequal, consider the following statements:
\begin{itemize}
\item $(a_1)$ $AB \parallel DE$. \quad $(a_2)$ $AE = BD$.
\item $(b_1)$ $BC \parallel EF$. \quad $(b_2)$ $BF = CE$.
\item $(c_1)$ $CD \parallel FA$. \quad $(c_2)$ $CA = DF$.
\end{itemize}
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] Show that if all six of these statements are true then the hexagon is cyclic.
\item[(b)] Prove that, in fact, any five of the six statements suffice.
\end{enumerate}
